# GenomeChain — Branch & Commit Rules for Claude

## Branch Strategy

| Branch  | Purpose                        | Who touches it          |
|---------|--------------------------------|-------------------------|
| `main`  | Production — DO NOT TOUCH      | Never push directly     |
| `master`| Staging — DO NOT TOUCH         | Never push directly     |
| `dev`   | Integration branch             | Merge feature PRs here  |
| `feat/*`| Feature work                   | Your working branch     |
| `fix/*` | Bug fixes                      | Your working branch     |
| `docs/*`| Documentation only             | Your working branch     |

## Workflow

1. Always branch off `dev`:
   ```bash
   git checkout dev && git pull origin dev
   git checkout -b feat/<your-feature>
   ```

2. Commit often. Every meaningful change = one commit.

3. Push and open PR targeting `dev` (never master/main):
   ```bash
   git push -u origin feat/<your-feature>
   gh pr create --base dev
   ```

4. All PRs must target `dev`. Never open a PR to `master` or `main`.

## Commit Format

```
type(scope): short description

feat     – new feature
fix      – bug fix
docs     – documentation only
chore    – config, deps, tooling
refactor – restructure without behaviour change
test     – tests only
```

Examples:
```
feat(contracts): add StudyRegistry joinStudy logic
fix(frontend): handle missing genome key gracefully
docs(arkiv): add friction report for prize submission
chore(deps): bump @worldcoin/minikit-js to 1.4.0
```

## End every commit with:
```
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
```

## Never commit:
- `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env*.local`
- `packages/contracts/.env`
- Private keys, API keys, mnemonics
- `node_modules/`, `.next/`, `artifacts/`, `typechain-types/`

## Prize Track Context (3 tracks only)
- **World** — MiniKit mini app, World ID Orb verification
- **Arkiv** — genome + medical record metadata on Arkiv Rabdi testnet
- **EF Anon-RPC** — all chain reads through WorldChain Anon RPC

Dropped: 0G, ENS, Definitive — do not re-add these.

## Contract Addresses (WorldChain Sepolia, chain 4801)
See `packages/frontend/.env.local` and `README.md` — all 7 contracts deployed.
Do not redeploy unless explicitly asked.
